{
 "version": 1,
 "title": "Advanced 6 \u00b7 Sample & hold, and slew",
 "text": "A Sample & Hold takes a snapshot of a signal on each trigger and holds it until the next. With nothing plugged into its IN it snapshots its own noise: a new random value on every tick of the Clock. Into a resonant filter, that's the bubbling 'computer' sound. Then a Slew smooths the jumps into glides: the same random movement, but liquid instead of stepped. Hold a note and listen.\n\nTry: pull the Slew out (plug the Sample & Hold straight into the filter's CUTOFF): steps; the Slew's RISE and FALL (longer: lazier); the Clock's 1/16 into the TRIGGER (faster); an LFO's OUT into the Sample & Hold's IN (it samples the LFO: a staircase that climbs and falls); send the Sample & Hold to the oscillator's FM instead, with FM small (0.1): a random melody.",
